      "text": "To determine which number between 1 and 15 has the greatest number of divisors, we need to calculate the number of divisors for each number in the range. We can do this by finding the prime factorization of each number and then using the formula for finding the number of divisors. The formula for the number of divisors of a number \\( n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\) is \\((e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\\).\n\nLet's calculate the number of divisors for each number from 1 to 15.\n\n1. For \\( n = 1 \\):\n   \\[\n   1 = 1^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2\n   \\]\n\n2. For \\( n = 2 \\):\n   \\[\n   2 = 2^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. For \\( n = 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   3 = 3^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n\n4. For \\( n = 4 \\):\n   \\[\n   4 = 2^2 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n\n5. For \\( n = 5 \\):\n   \\[\n   5 = 5^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n\n6. For \\( n = 6 \\):\n   \\[\n   6 = 2^1 \\times 3^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = (1 + 1)(1 + 1) = 2 \\times 2 = 4\n   \\]\n\n7. For \\( n = 7 \\):\n   \\[\n   7 = 7^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n\n8. For \\( n = 8 \\):\n   \\[\n   8 = 2^3 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 3 + 1 = 4\n   \\]\n\n9. For \\( n = 9 \\):\n   \\[\n   9 = 3^2 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n\n10. For \\( n = 10 \\):\n    \\[\n    10 = 2^1 \\times 5^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = (1 + 1)(1 + 1) = 2 \\times 2 = 4\n    \\]\n\n11. For \\( n = 11 \\):\n    \\[\n    11 = 11^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n    \\]\n\n12. For \\( n = 12 \\):\n    \\[\n    12 = 2^2 \\times 3^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = (2 + 1)(1 + 1) = 3 \\times 2 = 6\n    \\]\n\n13. For \\( n = 13 \\):\n    \\[\n    13 = 13^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = 2 + 1 = 3\n    \\]\n\n14. For \\( n = 14 \\):\n    \\[\n    14 = 2^1 \\times 7^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = (1 + 1)(1 + 1) = 2 \\times 2 = 4\n    \\]\n\n15. For \\( n = 15 \\):\n    \\[\n    15 = 3^1 \\times 5^1 \\Rightarrow \\text{number of divisors} = (1 + 1)(1 + 1) = 2 \\times 2 = 4\n    \\]\n\nNow, let's list the number of divisors for each number:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|c}\n\\text{Number} & \\text{Number of Divisors} \\\\\n\\hline\n1 & 2 \\\\\n2 & 3 \\\\\n3 & 3 \\\\\n4 & 3 \\\\\n5 & 3 \\\\\n6 & 4 \\\\\n7 & 3 \\\\\n8 & 4 \\\\\n9 & 3 \\\\\n10 & 4 \\\\\n11 & 3 \\\\\n12 & 6 \\\\\n13 & 3 \\\\\n14 & 4 \\\\\n15 & 4 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nFrom the table, we can see that the number 12 has the greatest number of divisors, which is 6.\n\nThus, the number with the greatest number of divisors is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
