      "text": "To determine which number between 1 and 15 has the greatest number of divisors, we need to find the number of divisors for each integer in this range. We can achieve this by writing a function to compute the number of divisors of a given number and then applying this function to each number between 1 and 15.\n\nHere's the step-by-step plan:\n1. Define a function to calculate the number of divisors of a given number.\n2. Iterate through each number from 1 to 15, calculate the number of divisors for each, and keep track of the number with the maximum number of divisors.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n```python\ndef count_divisors(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the number of divisors of n.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\n# Find the number with the greatest number of divisors from 1 to 15\nmax_divisors = 0\nnumber_with_max_divisors = None\n\nfor number in range(1, 16):\n    divisors_count = count_divisors(number)\n    if divisors_count > max_divisors:\n        max_divisors = divisors_count\n        number_with_max_divisors = number\n\nprint(number_with_max_divisors)\n```\n```output\n8\n```\nThe number between 1 and 15 that has the greatest number of divisors is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
